  "narrative": "The new validation results materially strengthen the leading claims. All estimates are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction: for direction -1, a positive estimate means stronger dependency/more negative score in the exposed group; for direction +1, a positive estimate means weaker dependency/less negative score in the exposed group.\n\nH7 is independently validated. The discovery result for SMARCA4-loss cells having stronger SMARCA2 dependency was +0.784 with a 95% discovery interval +0.765 to +0.803; validation gave +0.805 with an independent interval +0.774 to +0.836. The two estimates are nearly identical and both are extremely large relative to the SMARCA2 dependency-score scale. I therefore keep H7 accepted and close its investigation.\n\nH13 is now independently validated. This is the reversed, biologically counterintuitive claim that KEAP1-loss cells have weaker NFE2L2 dependency, i.e. a higher/less negative dependency_NFE2L2 score. Discovery was +0.796; validation was +0.802 with an independent interval +0.775 to +0.829. Because H10 was the original opposite-direction claim, validation evidence also strengthens rejection of H10. Thus H13 is accepted and closed as a dataset-supported association, while H10 remains rejected and closed. This does not imply causality or biological generality; it means the measured direction is consistent under independent validation in this dataset.\n\nH17 is independently validated. The WRN/MSI-high association, restricted to a comparator population with mutation burden at least 4, was +0.787 in discovery and +0.819 in validation with an independent interval +0.769 to +0.868. This supports the interpretation that the WRN association is not merely an artifact of comparing MSI-high cells against very low-mutation-burden cells. It also indirectly supports H9, but H9 itself is the unrestricted MSI-high effect and has not yet received direct independent validation, so I leave H9 accepted but active as a future validation candidate.\n\nTaken together, the four leading associations are: TP53-wild-type cells have much stronger USP7 dependency (H6, discovery +0.802, not yet independently validated); SMARCA4-loss cells have much stronger SMARCA2 dependency (H7, accepted and independently validated); MSI-high cells have much stronger WRN dependency (H9, accepted with multiple robustness checks and validation of related restricted analysis H17); and KEAP1-loss cells have weaker NFE2L2 dependency/higher dependency score (H13, accepted and independently validated). Each accepted effect is approximately 0.75 to 0.85 on the dependency-score scale, corresponding to roughly two to three outcome standard deviations. Because many dependency scores have negative means, I judged the 10% relative-difference benchmark primarily through effect size and uncertainty rather than as a literal percent change in a negative quantity; these effects clearly exceed scientifically meaningful thresholds within the supplied dataset.\n\nThe negative and null findings are now also more interpretable. Same-target dependency claims were not supported: KRAS mutation did not predict KRAS dependency, BRAF V600E did not predict BRAF dependency, EGFR amplification did not predict EGFR dependency after conditional checks, and ERBB2 amplification did not predict ERBB2 dependency. PIK3CA mutation did not predict STAT3 dependency. MYC amplification did not predict POLR2A dependency, and the high-MYC-expression refinement of RPL11 was also null. TP53 loss did not predict MDM2 dependency and did not support a meaningful DHX9 association in the hypothesized direction. MSI-high did not predict KIF18A dependency. KRAS mutation did not show the predicted weaker RIT1 dependency among BRAF-wild-type cells. Interaction tests found no reliable evidence that ARID1A loss modifies the SMARCA4-loss/SMARCA2 effect, that TP53 loss modifies the KEAP1-loss/NFE2L2 effect, that ARID1A loss modifies the USP7/TP53 association, or that TP53 loss modifies the SMARCA4/SMARCA2 association.\n\nThe main remaining uncertainty is no longer statistical significance for the leading effects but scientific interpretation and generalization. KEAP1-loss cells having weaker NFE2L2 dependency is consistent and now validated, but its mechanistic meaning is not established by this dataset. Similarly, TP53-wild-type cells having stronger USP7 dependency could reflect selective pressure, scoring artifacts, co-alteration structure, or real biological dependency; the data show an association, not a causal mechanism. Likewise, all conclusions remain limited to the supplied lung cell-line population and measured assays; they should not be described as clinical biomarkers or generalizable causal rules.\n\nThe most informative next step is to pursue independent validation for the remaining accepted main effect H6 USP7/TP53-wild-type dependency, and then for H9 WRN/MSI-high if validation capacity remains. Because only one new validation request is available at each appraise cycle, H6 is the higher priority because it is a large accepted main effect lacking direct independent replication. In parallel, I registered non-KY-library refinements of the four leading associations to test whether the effects generalize across the major screen-library context rather than being confined to the KY subset. The active discovery queue should continue to cover unresolved outcomes and predictors, but direct validation of H6 and H9 should take precedence when appropriate.",
  "research_notes": "Current validated accepted main associations: H7 SMARCA4 loss stronger SMARCA2 dependency (validated R13); H13 KEAP1 loss weaker NFE2L2 dependency/higher score (validated R38; H10 opposite rejected). H17 WRN MSI-high restricted to mutation_burden >=4 accepted and validated (R39), supporting but not directly validating H9. Accepted main still unvalidated: H6 TP53 WT stronger USP7 dependency; H9 MSI-high stronger WRN dependency. Robustness accepted/closed: H14/H15 SMARCA4 effect with and without ARID1A loss; H16 no ARID1A interaction; H18 USP7 in MYC-amplified; H21 USP7 in KY; H22 NFE2L2 in KY; H23 SMARCA2 in KY; H31 NFE2L2 in STK11 WT; H33 WRN in adenocarcinoma; H41 NFE2L2 in adenocarcinoma; H42 WRN in TP53 WT. Interaction null: H43 no ARID1A modification of USP7/TP53; H44 no TP53 modification of SMARCA4/SMARCA2; H25 no KEAP1-by-TP53 interaction. Rejected/null closed include KRAS/BRAF/EGFR/ERBB2 direct-target claims, MDM2/TP53, ARID1A alone, PIK3CA/STAT3, MYC/POLR2A, MYC/RPL11 high-expression, DHX9/TP53, KIF18A/MSI, RIT1/KRAS BRAF WT, TMED10/ERBB2. Deferred low-priority: H20, H24, H37, H38, H39, H40. Next validation priority: H6, then H9. Next discovery priority: non-KY-library robustness proposals for H6/H7/H9/H13 plus existing H26-H32, H34-H36, H52."
}

