  "narrative": "The highest-value next comparisons are context-robustness tests for the four large accepted associations rather than another broad search for new predictors. The current supported pattern in the supplied lung-cell-line dataset is very strong for TP53 wild-type stronger USP7 dependency (H6), SMARCA4-loss stronger SMARCA2 dependency (H7, independently validated), MSI-high stronger WRN dependency (H9, with robustness checks and validation of the higher-TMB-restricted version H17), and KEAP1-loss weaker NFE2L2 dependency / higher NFE2L2 score (H13, independently validated). All estimates are interpreted under the signed convention: direction -1 means a positive estimate is stronger dependency / more negative score in the exposed group; direction +1 means a positive estimate is weaker dependency / higher score in the exposed group.\n\nI registered four adherent-culture robustness tests. The scientific hypothesis is that if the accepted associations are not merely artifacts of a few non-adherent culture contexts or cell-line screen conditions, they should retain near-full effect size among the large adherent subset. For USP7, TP53 wild-type cells are expected to remain more dependent than TP53-loss cells, so direction -1 with anticipated raw signed positive. For SMARCA2, SMARCA4-loss cells are expected to remain more dependent than SMARCA4-intact cells. For WRN, MSI-high cells are expected to remain more dependent than MSI-low cells. For NFE2L2, KEAP1-loss cells are expected to remain less dependent, i.e. have a higher/less negative score, so direction +1. Plausible alternatives are that an association is driven by non-adherent or low-frequency culture contexts, or that culture mode is correlated with screen quality or a distinct biological subgroup. If the adherent estimate remains around 0.75 to 0.85, that would materially strengthen interpretation as a broad dataset association. If it collapses toward zero, the effect should be interpreted as context-specific and not generalizable across the measured culture settings.\n\nI deferred several currently active lower-priority claims to keep the next analysis focused. H27 and H28 are lower-priority because related mechanistic checks for KIF18A and MYC/RPL11 have already produced small or near-null results. H29 is lower-priority because EGFR amplification direct-target and conditional claims have already been rejected. H32, H34, H35, and H36 test lineage-subtype robustness for effects that are either already independently validated or already supported in adenocarcinoma and other subsets; adenocarcinoma is the majority subset and therefore adds less information than validation or the new culture-context tests. H52 is deferred because high-MYC-expression refinement of POLR2A is closely related to the high-MYC RPL11 test, which was null, while direct MYC-POLR2A was also null.\n\nThe next appraise cycle should prioritize independent validation of H6 if a validation request can be paired with the new results. H6 is the only large accepted main effect lacking direct independent validation; H7 and H13 are already validated, and H9 has strong validation-adjacent evidence through H17 but still needs direct independent replication. If H6 validates and validation capacity remains, H9 should be the next validation target. All conclusions remain associations within this dataset and its measured assays, not causal effects, clinical biomarker claims, or externally generalizable mechanisms.",
  "research_notes": "Accepted main effects: H6 TP53 WT stronger USP7 (unvalidated but huge); H7 SMARCA4 loss stronger SMARCA2 (validated); H9 MSI-high stronger WRN (accepted active, needs direct validation; H17 related restricted effect validated); H13 KEAP1 loss weaker NFE2L2/higher score (validated; H10 opposite rejected). Accepted robustness: H14/H15/H16 SMARCA4 robustness/no ARID1A interaction; H18 USP7 in MYC-amplified; H21 USP7 KY; H22 NFE2L2 KY; H23 SMARCA2 KY; H31 NFE2L2 STK11 WT; H33 WRN adenocarcinoma; H41 NFE2L2 adenocarcinoma; H42 WRN TP53 WT; H43/H44/H25 interaction nulls. Null/rejected direct-target and mechanistic claims: KRAS, BRAF, EGFR, ERBB2 same-target; MDM2/TP53; ARID1A alone; PIK3CA/STAT3; MYC/POLR2A; MYC high-expression RPL11; DHX9/TP53 tiny opposite; KIF18A/MSI; RIT1/KRAS BRAF WT; TMED10/ERBB2. New active priority queue after deferrals: H6, H9, H26, H30, H54-H57, plus four new adherent-culture robustness proposals. Next appraise: request validation for H6 if possible; then H9. Interpret accepted effects as dataset associations, not causality or clinical generalizability. Deferral rationale: prioritize validation/culture robustness over redundant lineage-subtype or low-prior-null predictor checks."
